---
description: Cross-session memory management via recall/remember tools
alwaysApply: true
globs: []
---

MANDATORY always call <prefix>_recall(query=<context>) before searching, instead of guessing,
also when resuming a session, or getting a new prompt. Always recall HOW-TOs when you cannot
locate a system path, repo, file, URL, or when you misused API call or a command line arguments.
Read available <prefix>_search, <prefix>_recall, <prefix>_remember tool names from
knowledge://stores of rag-knowledge mcp.

MANDATORY always use progressive disclosure for <prefix>_recall():
* detail_level="L0" - scan titles and note saved_at
* detail_level="L1" - only for relevant items by the L0 topic. Narrow scope with
  saved_after=saved_at-1h, saved_before=saved_at+1h (8h, 1d, 1m when retrying).
  Use timezone-aware ISO stamps (e.g. 2026-08-26T10:22:00+00:00); date-only
  fails with naive vs aware compare.
* (optional) detail_level="L2" - for full content of relevant 1-2 items only, by the time window and
  elaborated query from L1 and L0 results. Always do for recall(), optional for search().

Example: narrow scope when L1 hides good results shown at L0, or L2 hides wanted Lx result:
  recall(query="RAG summarizer tests", detail_level="L0")
  → sees good item from 2026-08-26 among noise
  recall(query="RAG summarizer tests", detail_level="L1", saved_after="2026-08-26", saved_before="2026-08-27")
  → narrows to that day, gets wanted overview from 2026-08-26T12:00
  recall(query="REFERENCE RESULTS granite", detail_level="L2", saved_after="2026-08-26T11:00",
  saved_before="2026-08-26T13:00")
  → full content of the exact memory

MANDATORY always save memories via <prefix>_remember(content=..., category=...)
whenever:
- User states a preference, corrects a mistake or confirms anything
- A significant architectural decision was made by a user
- You learned conventions, a path, a source or a URL
- A workflow succeeds with confirmed outcome
- A tool or issued command succeeds with expected results.
Allowed memories categories: preference, decision, learning, correction, context, workflow.

Remember() dedup: write-time by cosine similarity.
Recall() dedup: suppresses already-returned memories within a session.
Session identity precedence: <prefix>_recall(client_id=...) > MCP transport
client_id > server-generated session_id. Restarting server resets the latter.

Use different client_id per sub-session for coherent view (same top results recalled).
Use fixed client_id across sub-sessions for alternative opinions
(suppressing already-returned memories forcing diverse results).
